tion, beats everything.\n        13. Quadplex set: a quad with two single cards OR two pairs attached.\n        Use the EXACT card symbols provided in the Valid Moves list.\n        Prepare a valid JSON object like {"cards": ["♠3", "♥3"]} for your answer, along with your explanation and reason. If you pass, output: {"cards": []}\n        \n        Now is your turn, to your best ability, choose your move to maximize your chances of winning.\n        Please briefly evaluate a few proimsing moves, provide reason for your final choice, and output the action with specified format.\n        Your response format should be:\n        Evaluation: [Your Evaluation]\n        Reason: [Your Reason]\n        Answer: [Your Answer]\n    ', 'user_prompt': "You are playing as a peasant. Your aim is to be the play out all your cards before the landlord does, OR help your teammate (the other peasant) play out their cards before the landlord does. If the landlord plays out all cards first, you lose.\nYou are a Peasant. The Previous Player (Left) is the Landlord (ENEMY). The Next Player (Right) is your TEAMMATE (Peasant). You must cooperate with your teammate to beat the Landlord. The objective is to empty your hand before the landlord does, or help your teammate empty their hand before the landlord does.\n\nYour Hand: ♥7 ♣9 ♦J ♠A\nLast Play to Beat: ♠9\n--- Game History (Recent) ---\nTurn 3 (You): ♠3 ♦3\nTurn 4 (Next Player): ♣4 ♦4\nTurn 4 (Prev Player): ♥6 ♦6\nTurn 4 (You): Pass\nTurn 5 (Next Player): ♠7 ♣7\nTurn 5 (Prev Player): ♥8 ♦8\nTurn 5 (You): Pass\nTurn 6 (Next Player): ♣Q ♦Q\nTurn 6 (Prev Player): ♥K ♣K\nTurn 6 (You): Pass\nTurn 7 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 7 (Prev Player): ♠4 ♥4 ♠10 ♥10 ♣10\nTurn 7 (You): Pass\nTurn 8 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 8 (Prev Player): ♠9\n--- Player Info ---\nCards Held by Next Player (Right) [Peasant (Teammate)]: 11\nCards Held by Prev Player (Left) [Landlord (Opponent)]: 4\n--- Cards Remaining Unknown (Card Counting) ---\n(Format explanation: 'Rank: 