ure landlord play or support my teammate.\n\nThus, ♦J is the optimal play — it continues pressure without waste.\n\nReason: Playing ♦J beats the landlord’s ♠9 efficiently, preserving my stronger ♠A for a future critical moment. Given the landlord is near victory, interrupting their progress now with a minimal sufficient card gives me and my teammate more chances to coordinate later. Passing would surrender control, risking immediate loss.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦J"]}'}
